 "final_text_tail": " in the cache path of `to_datetime`. Once a categorical input has more than 50 unique values, `to_datetime` builds a date cache and calls `_convert_and_box_cache`. That function maps the categorical through `Series(arg, ...).map(cache_array)`, which keeps the result categorical. `_box_as_indexlike` then wraps that categorical as-is, so the output stays categorical instead of becoming datetime.\n\n```json\n{\"files\": [\"pandas/core/tools/datetimes.py\", \"pandas/core/tools/datetimes.py\", \"pandas/core/tools/datetimes.py\"], \"functions\": [\"_convert_and_box_cache\", \"_box_as_indexlike\", \"to_datetime\"]}\n```",
